{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789210729,"nonce":"LjfxwNWwTz6dscomywCcFXCDo4o=","title":"aarch64 frame pointer convention fix","message":"Fixed; see git log for the landing commit. Record migrated from session memory 2026-09-12.\n\n\n- **Frame pointer convention**: x29 = sp (standard aarch64), positive spill offsets\n- **Shadow store removal**: replaced with JIT_FRAME_STACK + precise safepoint scanning\n- **Reserved x20**: JitContext pointer, eliminates TLS in inline IC\n- **Inline IC**: kind=1 (leaf JIT), kind=4 (native), kind=5 (getter), kind=6 (non-leaf JIT)\n- **#[naked] wren_call_N wrappers**: capture (x29, x30) for GC frame registration\n- **Precise safepoint scanning**: return address in JIT_FRAME_STACK identifies active safepoint\n- **Nonleaf JIT dispatch**: removed interpreter fallback gate (nonleaf_moving_gc_safe)\n- **Constructor compilation**: kind=3 IC now calls record_call + poll_compilations\n- **Compilation queue**: background compilations queued instead of dropped\n\n- **Interpreter constructor JIT dispatch**: calling call_constructor_sync from the interpreter's inline Method::Constructor handler corrupts field values. Works correctly when called from dispatch_method (JIT caller path). Root cause: unclear interaction between arg_vals, poll_compilations, and mid-construction compilation transition.\n- **Double allocation**: fixed by checking JIT before allocating instance\n- **Conservative GC scanning**: replaced with precise per-safepoint scanning using return addresses\n\n| Benchmark | WrenLift | Std Wren | Ratio |\n|-----------|----------|----------|-------|\n| fib | 0.027s | 0.17s | 6.3x faster |\n| method_call | 0.037s | 0.085s | 2.3x faster |\n| binary_trees | 4.3s | 0.97s | 4.4x slower |\n| delta_blue | 0.23s | 0.096s | 2.4x slower |","files":null}]}